00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.700
Nagasaki was selected to become target city number two.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:38.970
Exactly three days after Hiroshima, a B-29 set out for Nagasaki.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.400
Instructions were precise.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:45.430
To the north, Japan's greatest torpedo plant.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.320
To the south, steel and arms works

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.460
were located in the heart of the city.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.590
The bomb was aimed midway between the two plants

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.170
to cause greatest possible damage.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.890
Because the plants were located in a valley,

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:59.980
surrounding hills shielded most...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.820
residential areas and concentrated the damage on the industrial section.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:10.220
At 10.58, the morning of August 9th, the bomb was exploded above the city and in the towering

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:12.580
mushroom Japan could read its doom.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.130
This was more than a routine bombing.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.880
It was the funeral pyre of an aggressor nation.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:23.000
The bomb had been purposely exploded high so that the greatest part of its radioactive

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.160
material was dissipated in the stratosphere.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:39.810
From the air, the skeletons of the Mitsubishi plants made evident that Nagasaki's war-making power was totally destroyed.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:48.650
For the valley area of little more than three square miles, blast and fire reduced the industrial plants and surrounding buildings to blackened rubble.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:59.860
The Mitsubishi steel and arms works extended almost a mile in length.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:04.280
Before the blast, these were modern buildings, constructed like our own American factories.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:10.940
Closer examination of the ruins shows the same complete destruction that characterized the ruins of Hiroshima.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:15.550
Damage to equipment and machinery used in the manufacture of naval rifles,

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:21.990
AA guns, and heavy artillery was such that even if Japan had determined to commit suicide by continuing resistance,

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:24.670
she could not have salvaged much from the ruins.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:29.070
Smokestacks bent, but did not break before the blast.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:35.360
And roads were unaffected, people using them without ill effect shortly after the explosion.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:47.390
